          <Pad Id="KQUlMqmzKY3PoYWgV4PT5F" Bounds="-620,-60,540,1100" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="04 - The shortest line between.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Move the mouse around the shape. An orange line connects your cursor to the nearest point&#xD;&#xA;on the polygon, a dot marks where it lands, and Distance is the length of exactly that&#xD;&#xA;line. Distance is not just a number - it is a place, and now you can see it.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WATCH THE ANCHOR. Along an edge it slides smoothly. At a corner it stops and waits while&#xD;&#xA;you swing past, then commits to the next edge. Nobody programmed that behaviour here -&#xD;&#xA;it falls out of what 'nearest' means.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;STEP INSIDE. Distance snaps to zero and the line has nowhere to go - the two nearest&#xD;&#xA;points coincide. This is where chapter 03 and chapter 04 turn out to be the same fact:&#xD;&#xA;Contains true means Distance zero. Two questions, one geometry.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE BRIDGE, CROSSED THE OTHER WAY. Chapters 01-03 turned Vector2 into Coordinate. Here&#xD;&#xA;Nearest Points hands back Coordinates, and Split + Vector (Join) turn them into Vector2&#xD;&#xA;again so Skia can draw them. The boundary between your graphics world and geometry is a&#xD;&#xA;door, not a wall, and it opens both ways.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;PLAY&#xD;&#xA;  Circle a corner slowly and watch the anchor wait, then jump.&#xD;&#xA;  Hover the notch: the anchor picks whichever wall is truly closer, however it looks.&#xD;&#xA;  Wire Distance somewhere - a Radius, a volume, a blur. Proximity as a live signal is&#xD;&#xA;  half of interactive spatial design.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT HAPPENED?&#xD;&#xA;  Distance here is in canvas units and it is honest, because you own the space. On&#xD;&#xA;  longitude and latitude the same node returns degrees - a diagonal across a degree grid,&#xD;&#xA;  not metres over the ground. Act II makes that trap visible on the earth.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;GIS WORDS&#xD;&#xA;  distance          the length of the shortest line between two geometries&#xD;&#xA;  nearest points    the pair of points that line runs between&#xD;&#xA;  proximity         the analysis family these two belong to&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;CREATIVE CONNECTION&#xD;&#xA;  This is a distance field, sampled at one point - the SDF idea graphics people already&#xD;&#xA;  carry, aimed at real shapes instead of implicit ones.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THIS PATCH USES ONE PACKAGE, VL.NetTopologySuite, which is normally a reason to live in&#xD;&#xA;that package's own help folder rather than here. It is the exemption written into this&#xD;&#xA;pack's rules: the geometry act runs on that package alone, and a course with a hole in&#xD;&#xA;its opening act is worse than a node appearing in two places.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;NEXT - three directions, no order:&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 05             grow a shape - geometry that generates geometry&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 03             the yes/no version of this question&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 06             the earth, when you are ready for it">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
        </Canvas>
